Here is the root cause:
The root cause of the bug is that the OP-TEE node was present in the kernel device tree but did not have a corresponding reserved memory region declared. This led to the kernel misinterpreting the end of DDR as free memory, which was already in use by OP-TEE. Consequently, when the kernel attempted to access the CMA region, it caused an error raised by OP-TEE due to memory conflicts.

